Paste this entire script into one Google Colab cell, or upload it and run:

    %run /content/HXC_NOVEL_STRUCTURE_INVENTOR_COLAB.py

This system searches arbitrary finite binary-operation tables rather than only
affine formulas. It constructs candidate tables with a guaranteed nontrivial
automorphism, deduplicates them up to isomorphism, rejects familiar reference
structures, discovers laws and counterexamples, assigns fresh Unicode glyphs,
and emits a Lean 4 proof-carrying structure certificate.

Novelty is certified relative to:
  * the explicit reference library;
  * all isomorphism classes encountered in the current search;
  * the selected law fingerprint among surviving candidates.

That is a rigorous finite novelty claim, not a claim that the structure has
never appeared anywhere in the mathematical literature.
"""

